	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the support user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to have the role "Agent"
	And I assign the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "Provisioning - US"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
